# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Philipp Thölke et al. (2022). TorchMD-NET: Equivariant Transformers for Neural Network based Molecular Potentials.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2202.02541  arXiv:2202.02541v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2202.02541v2 (sha256 34842c95d3dd202e...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 205 (Method/model). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/tholke2022.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the equivariant Transformer of TorchMD-NET (introduced
# here; TorchMD-ET in the registry) and its energy and force errors on the
# eight MD17 molecules (Table 2), the CCSD/CCSD(T) MD17 trajectories
# (Table 8), the QM9 U0 target (Table 1) and ANI-1 (Fig. 2). The other QM9
# targets, the reduced-size ET variants (Table 7), the hydrogen ablation
# (Table 5) and values quoted from other papers are not encoded.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
