###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Training on two NVIDIA RTX 2080 Ti GPUs: 16 h for QM9, 10 h for MD17 and
# 83 h for ANI-1 (App. A). Inference on an NVIDIA V100: 11.7 ms (ET-large)
# and 9.4 ms (ET-small) per batch of 50 QM9 molecules for the forward pass,
# 48.5 and 39.0 ms with forces (Sec. 3.3, Table 3). The batch timings give
# no atom count, so no per-atom time is derived; the ET-small timing is of
# the MD17-sized architecture on QM9 molecules and is held in the encoding
# input.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - TorchMD-NET 'builds on top of the Transformer architecture' (Sec. 1) and is compared with the SE(3)-Transformer (App. A); neither is a registry MLIP method, so no derivation edge is recorded.
# - The QM9 and ANI-1 models are trained on energies only (QM9 one model per target); only the U0 target of QM9 is encoded. The ANI-1 MAE (0.012 eV) is read from the bar label of Fig. 2.
# - MD17 results are means over three random splits, CCSD/CCSD(T) results over two; the CCSD/CCSD(T) runs use 'the same training protocol as used for the original MD17 dataset' (App. I); their hyperparameters are not restated and are not encoded.
# - The PaiNN-sized and NequIP-sized ET variants (Table 7) and the models trained without hydrogen (Table 5) are not encoded.
# - The DFT/CC levels of the data sets are not described in this paper.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/tholke2022.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

